    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.compose - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.compose.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.compose()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Compose this graph with another graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.compose()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Compose this graph with another graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.compose()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Compose this graph with another graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCompose this graph with another graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L49810-L49924){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.compose(other)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Compose](../assets/graphs/compose.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The same G and H as for union, except that the shared fourth node is labeled D in G (accent) and D′ in H (teal). Compose merges nodes by id and keeps all four edges like union, but H wins the clash, so the result shows D′.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nSimilar to union, but the other graph's node attributes/labels take precedence over this\ngraph's. Useful when you want to merge updates from another graph.\n\nThe result contains every node and edge from both graphs, matched exactly as in\n`union()`: nodes by ID, edges by their pair of endpoint IDs. The only difference is who\nwins a clash. Wherever both graphs have a label, an attribute, or an edge weight for the\nsame node or edge, `other`'s value is used, and this graph's value is kept only where\n`other` has none. Typical uses:\n\n- applying a batch of corrections or updates (new labels, revised weights) to a base\n  network\n- layering a more recent or more trusted data source over an older one\n- adding edges and refreshing attributes in a single step\n\nIsolated nodes from both graphs are kept. Edges from this graph keep their IDs; edges\nonly `other` has get fresh IDs above every ID this graph has used. Neither input graph\nis modified.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[other]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The graph to compose with (its attributes take precedence). It must have the same\n    directedness as this graph. Its nodes are matched to this graph's nodes by ID, so a\n    node in `other` overrides the label and attributes of the node with the same ID here,\n    and an edge between the same pair of IDs overrides that edge's weight and attributes.\n    Attributes that only this graph has are preserved.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A new composed graph containing all nodes and edges from both graphs. It is weighted\n    if either input is weighted.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graphs have different directedness, or if the same label belongs to different\n    node IDs in the two graphs.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nCompose is a right-biased `union()`: the same edge set is produced, but wherever\nboth graphs carry a value for the same node or edge, the *other* graph's value\nwins. This makes it the natural primitive for applying updates or overlays to a\nbase graph without losing edges that were only in the base. Both operands must\nshare the same directedness.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~union`) \n\n:   Combine two graphs, keeping this graph's values.\n\n[](`~compose_all`) \n\n:   Apply any number of graphs in order.\n\n[](`~set_node_attrs`) \n\n:   Set an attribute on some or all nodes.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\n`compose()` is `union()` with the other graph's values winning, which makes it the way to\napply an update. Node \"A\" takes `team=\"blue\"` from `g2` and keeps `rank=1`, which `g2`\nlacks. The shared edge takes `g2`'s weight of `5.0`, and the edge `B--C` is added:\n\n::: {#1037ef83 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ng1 = ec.Graph()\ng1.add_nodes([(\"A\", {\"team\": \"red\", \"rank\": 1}), \"B\"])\ng1.add_edge(\"A\", \"B\", weight=1.0)\n\ng2 = ec.Graph()\ng2.add_nodes([(\"A\", {\"team\": \"blue\"}), \"B\", \"C\"])\ng2.add_edges([(\"A\", \"B\", 5.0), (\"B\", \"C\")])\n\nupdated = g1.compose(g2)\nupdated.get_node_df().select(\"label\", \"team\", \"rank\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (3, 3)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>label</th><th>team</th><th>rank</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>i64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;A&quot;</td><td>&quot;blue&quot;</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;B&quot;</td><td>null</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;C&quot;</td><td>null</td><td>null</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#0167a4d5 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nupdated.get_edge_df().select(\"source\", \"target\", \"weight\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (2, 3)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>source</th><th>target</th><th>weight</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>i64</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>5.0</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>null</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### A club update\n\n`ec.friends()` is a network of friendships in 2024 among the members of a chess club and a\nclimbing club. A year later the club secretary sends a new list, `snapshot=2`, with 8 new\nfriendships and one change of club: Vik has moved to chess. Composing takes both from the\nupdate. A union would add the friendships but keep Vik in climbing:\n\n::: {#7726feb7 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ny2024 = ec.friends()\nupdate = ec.friends(snapshot=2).set_node_attrs(\n    \"club\", \"Chess\", nodes=[\"Vik\"]\n)\n\nvik = y2024.get_id_from_label(\"Vik\")\n(\n    y2024.compose(update).get_node_attrs(\"club\")[vik],\n    y2024.union(update).get_node_attrs(\"club\")[vik],\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n('Chess', 'Climbing')\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nDrawn by club, the composed graph shows Vik in the chess color, though three of Vik's four\nfriends are climbers:\n\n::: {#65e28bc4 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ny2024.compose(update).plot(color_by=\"club\", label_by=\"label\", seed=2)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"34.7 -1.7 732.1 523.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"34.7\" y=\"-1.7\" width=\"732.1\" height=\"523.0\" fill=\"var(--ect-3239c383)\"/>\n<path d=\"M106.6,73.7 C107.9,76.1 111.3,75.3 114.3,87.9 C117.3,100.5 122.9,139.0 124.7,149.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4e79a7\" stroke-width=\"1.56\" stro